This doesn't work.  The occurrence of "1FOO*" does not refer to
the atomic symbol 1FOO* as a constant; it is treated as a variable,
just as "1X*" is.
	The essential problem is that we want to be able to
write any S-expression as a constant in a program, but some
S-expressions must be used to represent other things, such
as variables and procedure invocations.  To solve this problem
we invent a new notation: 1(QUOTE x)* in a program represents the
constant S-expression 1x*.  {Note 1QUOTE* Mapping}
Thus we can write our test as
"1(EQ X (QUOTE FOO))*".  Similarly,
.sp
.nofill
.spw 13
.block 1
