for encoding rather complex algorithms, including those of 
symbolic mathematics.  Often lists are used for representing such
structures as the set of coefficients of a polynomial or coordinates
of a space vector.  Many problems require one to perform an operation
on each element of a list and produce a new list of the results.
For example, it may be useful to make a list of the squares of each of
the elements in a vector.  We would write this as follows:
