/{Can George do better?}//Page 34/
.sp
	The problem here is that George needs access to the statistics
counter without giving that access to anyone else.  As described in the
next example George can make the counter an own variable, but how
can he get access to it?  One idea is that George can define 1MAPCAR*
in the following manner:
.sp
.nofill
.spw 13
.block 7
1     ((LAMBDA (N)
	      (PROGN (SETQ MAPCAR
			   (LAMBDA (F L)
				   (PROGN (SETQ N (+ N 1))
					  (OLDMAPCAR F L))))
		     (LAMBDA () N)))
      0)
.spw 16
.adjust
.sp
0
This expression defines 1MAPCAR* by 1SETQ0ing
(See {Note Driver Loop with Side Effects}.) it to an appropriate
procedure.  It then returns, as a value, an anonymous procedure which accesses
the value of the statistics counter.  If George saves this value and uses it
to get at the counter when he needs it, he will have isolated it completely
from everyone else!
