.sp
	A primitive operator might be a very complicated object
in a "real" LISP implementation; it would probably have machine-language code
within it.  We are not interested in the details of a particular host machine here;
we wish only to present a simple meta-circular definition
of 1PRIMOP* and 1PRIMOP-APPLY*.
We will notate the procedural object which is the value of 1CAR* (say) in
the initial top-level environment 1<THE-PRIMITIVE-PROCEDURES>*
as "1&CAR*".  This object has no interesting properties
except that it is EQ to itself and not to any other object.
The initial top-level environment therefore looks like:
.sp
.nofill
.spw 13
.block 2
1	(((CAR CDR EQ ATOM NULL NUMBERP + - * ...)
	  &CAR &CDR &EQ &ATOM &NULL &NUMBERP &+ &- &* ...))
