.sp
	We have implicitly thought of the 1RPLACA* operation
as modifying a cons so as to have a different car.
However, there is an interpretation in which 1RPLACA*
is thought of as modifying the 1CAR* operator.
Taking the car of an object always involves both the 1CAR* operator
and the object.  When we perform an 1RPLACA* on object denoted by 1FOO*,
all we can say is that the value of 1(CAR FOO)* may have changed.
It is not necessarily clear what aspect of that expression has changed.
Using this idea, we can express 1RPLACA* in terms of 1SETQ*
as in Figure N9.  Note that we depend on 1EQ* to distinguish
different results of 1CONS*.
