.sp
	We said "1EVAL*'s purpose is to determine the values
of expressions".  But what is the value of the expression 1(DRIVER)*?
It is certainly not an illegal or useless expression to evaluate,
yet it has no value.  The purpose of the expression is to cause
a certain process to be evolved; it is an "infinite loop",
which never returns.
This process includes side effects
(1READ* and 1PRINT*) through which it interacts with the user.
This situation arises because the system of interest is broken into
two parts with independent state: the computer and the user.
We will have more to say about this later.

